# AuroraOS Kconfig overlay: MiBand 8 without the QuickJS engine.
#
# Why this preset exists
# ----------------------
# Kconfig.miband enables CONFIG_QUICKJS_ENGINE by default, and MiBand 8 is the
# only board that does.  That means the `CONFIG_QUICKJS_ENGINE=n` path (root
# CMakeLists.txt does not add 3rdparty/quickjs sources, and any feature that
# depends on the JS heap must be compiled out) has no CI coverage at all.
#
# This preset keeps every other MiBand feature on, so the build also proves
# that the watch application and BLE stack do not implicitly require QuickJS.
#
# Note: the current MiBand image does not reference JsMiniProgramEngine (only
# runtime/js_app.hpp does, and no firmware target instantiates it), so the
# linker's --gc-sections drops the QuickJS objects either way and the linked
# image size is identical with and without the engine.  The gate therefore
# guards the source list / include path (the build must succeed when
# 3rdparty/quickjs is not compiled at all), not a distinct runtime path.
#
# Used by the `kconfig-matrix` job:
#   cmake -DAURORA_KCONFIG_OVERLAY=config/presets/miband8-no-quickjs.config ...
#
# CONFIG_QUICKJS_ENGINE is not set
